  <entry>
    <title>Data Workers&#39; Inquiry</title>
    <link href="https://parallels.lat/blog/2025-05-16-data-workers-inquiry/" />
    <updated>2025-05-16T17:09:00Z</updated>
    <id>https://parallels.lat/blog/2025-05-16-data-workers-inquiry/</id>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://data-workers.org/about/how-to-dwi/&quot;&gt;How we made Data Workers&#39; Inquiry&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A nice write-up of a workers&#39; inquiry project with data workers, researching the work that goes into training AI models (such as labelling datasets).
The inquiries are &lt;a href=&quot;https://data-workers.org/#Inquiries&quot;&gt;collected on the site&lt;/a&gt; and include workers from Kenya, Syria, Latin America
and Germany speaking about their working conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Among various outputs on the site, the article mentions that the project led to a &lt;a href=&quot;https://datalabelers.org/about/&quot;&gt;Data Labelers Association&lt;/a&gt; in Kenya.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title>Global video game history</title>
    <link href="https://parallels.lat/blog/2025-03-23-globl-video-game-history/" />
    <updated>2025-03-23T10:39:00Z</updated>
    <id>https://parallels.lat/blog/2025-03-23-globl-video-game-history/</id>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Enjoyed this article by Felipe Pepe: &lt;a href=&quot;https://felipepepe.medium.com/the-gentrification-of-video-game-history-dfe11f1e08ae&quot;&gt;The Gentrification of Video Game History&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;He provincialises US gaming history, highlighting games that were popular outside of the US and
ignored in typical histories of gaming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This helps us understand how games like Free Fire can reach 150 million daily users but have basically zero presence
in gamer circles &amp;amp; media — it’s a free-to-play battle royale mobile game created in Vietnam.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;He mentions a few interesting-sounding books:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://direct.mit.edu/books/monograph/4527/Real-GamesWhat-s-Legitimate-and-What-s-Not-in&quot;&gt;Real Games: What&#39;s legitimate and what&#39;s not in contemporary videogames&lt;/a&gt; by Mia Consalvo &amp;amp; Christopher A. Paul&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://direct.mit.edu/books/oa-monograph/5572/The-Videogame-Industry-Does-Not-ExistWhy-We-Should&quot;&gt;The Videogame Industry Does Not Exist&lt;/a&gt; by Brendan Keogh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</content>
  </entry>
