  <entry>
    <title>Kyle in Target Parking Lot</title>
    <link href="https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-15-kyle-in-target-parking-lot/" />
    <updated>2024-08-15T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <id>https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-15-kyle-in-target-parking-lot/</id>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;I came across this photo by Caroline Drake in an issue of Aperture in 2021 and it will pop into my head every couple of months. Probably with about the same frequency that I see a map of Idaho online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;picture&gt;&lt;source type=&quot;image/avif&quot; srcset=&quot;https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-15-kyle-in-target-parking-lot/YrCEf56VJR-608.avif 608w&quot;&gt;&lt;source type=&quot;image/webp&quot; srcset=&quot;https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-15-kyle-in-target-parking-lot/YrCEf56VJR-608.webp 608w&quot;&gt;&lt;img loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; src=&quot;https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-15-kyle-in-target-parking-lot/YrCEf56VJR-608.jpeg&quot; alt=&quot;Kyle in Target Parking Lot by Caroline Drake&quot; width=&quot;608&quot; height=&quot;790&quot;&gt;&lt;/picture&gt;
&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://aperture.org/prints/kyle-in-target-parking-lot-twin-falls-idaho-2016/&quot;&gt;Kyle in Target Parking Lot by Caroline Drake&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a side note, if you&#39;re in the UK you can read Aperture for free using the &lt;a href=&quot;https://libbyapp.com&quot;&gt;Libby library app&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title>Cartography / Typography #1</title>
    <link href="https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-14-cartography-typography-1/" />
    <updated>2024-08-14T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <id>https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-14-cartography-typography-1/</id>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;While doing some research on tyopgraphy in mapping, I found this table of cartographic lettering conventions on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.drjill.net&quot;&gt;Jill Saligoe-Simmel&#39;s website&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;picture&gt;&lt;source type=&quot;image/avif&quot; srcset=&quot;https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-14-cartography-typography-1/3ar3cx-IP7-523.avif 523w&quot;&gt;&lt;source type=&quot;image/webp&quot; srcset=&quot;https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-14-cartography-typography-1/3ar3cx-IP7-523.webp 523w&quot;&gt;&lt;img loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; src=&quot;https://parallels.lat/blog/2024-08-14-cartography-typography-1/3ar3cx-IP7-523.png&quot; alt=&quot;Cartographic Lettering Conventions&quot; width=&quot;523&quot; height=&quot;705&quot;&gt;&lt;/picture&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.drjill.net/map-fonts-article-1-the-basics-of-typography-for-cartography/&quot;&gt;Using Text on Maps: Typography in Cartography&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&#39;d love to read the context that goes with the table; it&#39;s taken from the Guild Handbook of Scientific Illustration, which is available on Archive.org but restricted to the US.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
